rom 0.18). Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause; investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt; do not redeploy v2.3.1 until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out. I'm retrying with the same idempotency key, so the incident can't be opened twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01E4vhe3CprKmzeY9uyYrhdn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Actions taken: (1) Identified v2.3.0 as the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are marked unhealthy; v2.2.9 is also healthy but older). (2) Rolled back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial failure, leaving the service in a mixed v2.3.0/v2.3.1 state). A second rollback attempt completed successfully. (3) Post-rollback status: us-east, us-west, and eu-west all on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002 (down from 0.18). Follow-ups: investigate the v2.3.1 failure root cause; investigate the orchestrator partial failure during the first rollback attempt; do not redeploy v2.3.1 until fixed.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and is healthy again. Error rate dropped from 0.18 to 0.002.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc were both unhealthy, so I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. Because v2.3.0 has already been healthy in production, no change-manager approval was needed.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across v2.3.0 and v2.3.1. I retried the same rollback once and it completed in all regions. The orchestrator error still needs investigating.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The first incident request timed out, so I retried with the same idempotency key. The incident was created once. The summary covers the rollback, the partial failure, the current state, and follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, look into the orchestrator error, and don't redeploy v2.3.1 until it's fixed.", "type": "text"}]}]}